@*
    Task 11.2 — the ASP.NET Core replacement for this plugin's web.config
    <system.web.webPages.razor><pages> element (Requirement 4.4).

    Identical in shape to tasks 10.1/10.2/11.1's; only the plugin's own Models namespace differs.
    See src/Plugins/Nop.Plugin.DiscountRules.CustomerRoles/Views/_ViewImports.cshtml for the full
    reasoning. In brief: all 20 plugins ship a byte-identical web.config declaring
    pageBaseType="Nop.Web.Framework.ViewEngines.Razor.WebViewPage" (→ the @inherits below, which
    is what makes T("…") and an unqualified @model resolve) plus four System.Web <namespaces>
    (→ the @using directives; System.Web.Mvc.Ajax has no ASP.NET Core counterpart and is
    dropped).

    It must sit at Views/ and inside the project file's Content/Link glob (Views\**\*.cshtml), so
    that this file and Configure.cshtml are linked into the SAME directory
    (/Plugins/Feed.GoogleShopping/Views/) — Razor resolves imports by walking up from the view's
    LINKED path. Linking the two inconsistently would make the imports silently not apply and the
    failure would look like a missing model type.

    NOTE Configure.cshtml declares `@model FeedGoogleShoppingModel` UNQUALIFIED, so the
    @using Nop.Plugin.Feed.GoogleShopping.Models below is not optional here — unlike 11.1's, where
    the plugin's @model is fully qualified.
*@
@inherits Nop.Web.Framework.ViewEngines.Razor.WebViewPage<TModel>

@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Html
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Http
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.Rendering
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Routing

@*
    Nop.Web.Framework carries HtmlExtensions (Html.NopLabelFor / NopEditorFor /
    NopDropDownListFor / RenderBootstrapTabHeader / RenderBootstrapTabContent),
    ViewCompatibilityExtensions and ChildActionExtensions. Extensions.SelectionIsNotPossible
    (used by the store dropdown below) is in the same namespace. One import covers all of them.
*@
@using Nop.Core.Infrastructure
@using Nop.Web.Framework
@using Nop.Web.Framework.UI
@using Nop.Plugin.Feed.GoogleShopping.Models

@*
    Tag helpers. 3.90 had none (they do not exist in MVC 5). Added for the same reason task 7.3
    added them to Nop.Web: the framework's form/validation tag helpers are the supported route to
    an anti-forgery token, and Html.BeginForm uses the same infrastructure.
*@
@addTagHelper *, Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.TagHelpers
